      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Adequacy of epidural-sacral anesthesia in proctological operations was studied. Sensometry occupies a special place among the methods, estimating the sacral anesthesia adequacy, owing the advantage of possibility for quantitative estimation of such an important index, as a patient reaction on external irritants, including such of a pain. Sensometry, according to A. K. Sangaylo method, using portative apparatus \"Nil - 3\" was conducted in 50 patients while proctological operations performance for estimation of various variants of sacral anesthesia efficacy. There was established, that sensometry constitutes the most informative quantitative method of estimation of the anesthesia adequacy."},
